# `PAINT-ORDER-CONSTRUCT`: the EXPERIMENTAL half of `918-withdrawn-plane-keyword`.
#
# `plane` is reached from the retired-keyword sweep, which runs AHEAD of the
# `GENRE-KEYWORD-ALLOWLIST` genre allowlist, so it answers the SAME message in every genre and
# abandons the line before its options are read. "Every genre" is a claim
# about all eight, and it is only checked if all eight are written down. The
# normative five are `918`'s three sections (`block`, `bitfield`, `table`)
# plus the `timing`/`signal` DIRECTIVES exercised there as a region inside a
# block section. This file is the rest of the claim, which cannot live in
# `cases/` because each section declares an EXPERIMENTAL genre:
#
#   flowchart   here                      statechart  here
#   timing      here — the genre HEADER, which is a different position from
#               the block opener `918` writes, the distinction `916` pins for
#               the `wave` -> `timing` rename in both positions
#   topology    241-topology-withdrawn-cells, alongside that genre's two
#               per-cell withdrawals — it is the genre where every authored
#               `plane` in the tree was actually written
#
# The `timing` section is the one worth having: it is a REGION genre and
# never declared a scene keyword, so nothing in it could be a per-genre
# withdrawal (`SCENE-KEYWORD-MEMBERSHIP`) and the message can only be arriving from the
# language-wide sweep. That is the difference between `SCENE-KEYWORD-MEMBERSHIP` and `PAINT-ORDER-CONSTRUCT` made
# observable rather than asserted.
#
# `flowchart` and `statechart` declare 0.2 because the genres do; `timing`
# is legal from 0.1 (spelled `wave` until 0.1, `TIMING-GENRE-NAMING`).
figdown 0.2 flowchart
node a "A"
plane over "Overlay"
flowline a -> a plane=over

figdown 0.2 statechart
state idle "IDLE"
plane over "Overlay"
transition idle -[tick]-> idle plane=over

figdown 0.1 timing
plane over "Overlay"
timing bus "Bus"
signal clk 0101
signal data ==.= z-index=1
